In my last game, I had 3 pet chameleons, all by accident (I would feed a
dog which would turn out to be a chameleon).

They were one of the BEST pets I ever had.  Much of the time, they
just jumped around being goblins or whatever, therefore not attacking
the creatures I was after for the experience, but when I wanted to
steal from a shop or kill a priest (I do that, because I don't know
anything better to do with opposite aligned priests), I just whisted
him in and when he was a mind flayer, dragon, minotaur, vamp lord, or
whatever he fealt was tough enough, he would kill the enemy (at no cost
to my AC or ESP).  I just stood by watching and blew the magic whistle
whenever he polymorphed back into a goblin (actually, I'm not sure, but
the conflict may have stopped as soon as he was too weak anyway).  

The best thing about this pet is that it is just SO easy to get.  There
are a half-dozen different monsters you can throw tripe to to tame, so
a chameleon polymorphs into one pretty regularly (just keep out of the
way until it does!) 

